  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nAmount= Rs. 13200 for 2 years\n\nAmount= Rs. 14520 for 3 years\n\n**Formula Used:**\n\nAmount= P(1+(R)/(100))^T\n\n**Calculations:**\n\nAccording to the questions,\n\n⇒ Amount= P(1+(R)/(100))^T\n\n⇒ 13200= P(1+(R)/(100))² .........................(1)\n\nSimilarly,\n\n⇒ Amount= P(1+(R)/(100))^T\n\n⇒ 14520= P(1+(R)/(100))³ .........................(2)\n\nDivide the eq (2) by eq (1), and we get\n\n⇒ (14520)/(13200)=(P(1+frac{R)/(100))³}{P(1+(R)/(100))²}\n\n⇒ (11)/(10)=1+(R)/(100)\n\n⇒ (11)/(10)-1=(R)/(100)\n\n⇒ (R)/(100)=(1)/(10)\n\n⇒ R= 10\n\n**Hence, The rate of interest per annum is 10%**",
